**Every push runs the committed pre-push hook, `.githooks/pre-push`, which refuses force pushes, remote ref deletions and updates over a remote commit this clone lacks. It is switched on per clone: a fresh clone runs `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` once, and a session runs the session-start check (`sh scripts/session-start.sh`) at pre-flight, which fails when `git config core.hooksPath` does not print `.githooks`.**
Why: `core.hooksPath` is clone-local config that git never copies, so a clone without the setup line pushes with no hook and nothing says so.

**Never pass `--no-verify` to git, and never set `core.hooksPath` on git's command line or in any other config scope; that escape hatch is the human's, typed in a terminal.**
Why: the hook stops mistakes, not a session set on getting around it: `--no-verify`, an edited hook file, `core.hooksPath` in another config scope and config set through the environment all skip it, and `.claude/settings.json` denies only the usual spellings.

**Write a precedent into this file the moment it is confirmed load-bearing, not at session end.**
Why: conversation history is not repo state, and a lesson left in scrollback is one context compaction away from lost.

