## Spec-Update Protocol

Run after every ship, in this order.

**1. Add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry with full detail (behavior, schema, files touched), rolling the oldest active entry verbatim into the open archive if the window is exceeded.**
Why: the changelog is the only record of what changed and why, and the roll keeps the active file readable.

**2. Update the `PRODUCT_SPEC.md` Feature Index row and the Current Feature Set subsection for every feature the ship touched.**
Why: the spec is where the next session learns current behavior; a stale spec is a wrong spec.

**3. On roadmap-related ships, remove or trim whatever shipped from `ROADMAP.md`; it only ever shrinks.**
Why: the roadmap specifies unbuilt state, so shipped detail there reads as work still owed.

**4. Run the scoped doc-contract check (`{{DOC_CONTRACT_CMD}}`) as its own command before the build and the full suite.**
Why: it runs in seconds, while a doc-shape failure found inside the full suite costs a second full run.

**Spec bullets state durable behavior, never implementation expressions: "hidden on archived orders", not "renders when `order.status !== 'archived'`".**
Why: expressions go stale silently on the next refactor with no typecheck to catch them; the cited version already points back to the code.

